Chapter: StringBuilderIndependence
  cites Foreword chapter StringBuilder

 The builder is a mutable record and appends in place, so the whole design
 rests on two builders started from sb-new being two records rather than one
 shared one. sb-new is a definition and not storage, so every mention of it
 re-materialises a fresh record with its own empty parts list. That is an
 assumption about how a zero-argument definition evaluates, and an assumption
 of that kind is exactly what this test exists to refuse to take on trust: if
 sb-new ever yielded one shared record, every builder in the program would
 accumulate every other builder's text and nothing else in the tree would
 notice.

 Two builders are started independently and given different text. Each must
 report only its own. A shared record shows up as either builder carrying the
 other's characters, and the length is checked as well as the text so that a
 builder which merely prints correctly cannot pass.

 We say:

Section: Probe

  sbi-two-from-new : Text
  sbi-two-from-new =
    let a = sb-append (sb-append sb-new "alpha") "-one"
    in let b = sb-append (sb-append sb-new "beta") "-two"
    in sb-to-text a & "|" & sb-to-text b

  sbi-lengths : Text
  sbi-lengths =
    let a = sb-append sb-new "abc"
    in let b = sb-append (sb-append sb-new "de") "fgh"
    in show (sb-length a) & "|" & show (sb-length b)

  sbi-threaded : Text
  sbi-threaded =
    let sb = sb-append (sb-append (sb-append sb-new "x") "y") "z"
    in sb-to-text sb & "|" & show (sb-length sb)

  sbi-empty-append : Text
  sbi-empty-append =
    let sb = sb-append (sb-append sb-new "keep") ""
    in sb-to-text sb & "|" & show (sb-length sb)

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    print-line-uni sbi-two-from-new
    print-line-uni sbi-lengths
    print-line-uni sbi-threaded
    print-line-uni sbi-empty-append
  end
